WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.020
A T-shirt shop prints custom shirts.

2
00:00:03.020 --> 00:00:06.230
To sell more, it has to lower its price.

3
00:00:06.230 --> 00:00:09.780
Sell 3 shirts, and its
profit is 16 dollars.

4
00:00:09.780 --> 00:00:12.760
Sell a fourth, and money still comes in.

5
00:00:12.760 --> 00:00:16.770
Total revenue rises from 42 to 48 dollars.

6
00:00:16.770 --> 00:00:20.080
Yet profit falls, to 14 dollars.

7
00:00:20.080 --> 00:00:22.750
So why would a business
stop making more when

8
00:00:22.750 --> 00:00:25.590
each extra sale still brings in money?

9
00:00:25.590 --> 00:00:28.480
In this mission, you'll
build a profit table and spot

10
00:00:28.480 --> 00:00:30.230
the point where it turns.

11
00:00:30.230 --> 00:00:32.890
Then you'll move output
up and down and find

12
00:00:32.890 --> 00:00:34.980
the top of the profit hill.

13
00:00:34.980 --> 00:00:37.690
Your mission: find the
rule that tells a firm

14
00:00:37.690 --> 00:00:39.310
exactly where to stop.
